input arrays reversed: sec 12.6: one key closes twice at one position, both successions anchored in one second and each named by a genesis; a succession to itself hands nothing off, so both are candidates, the continuation is the genesis with the bytewise-smallest entry_id, and BROKEN_CHAIN comes from both segments: the old reads the fork at seq 2, the new the two root geneses at seq 0. Here the entry met first has the larger id.
